<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mary II of England</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1662–1694</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Mary II was queen of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> and Ireland from 1689 to 1694, reigning jointly with her husband <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-iii-of-england">William III of Orange</a>. The Protestant elder daughter of James II, she was offered the throne with William after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/glorious-revolution">Glorious Revolution</a>, and they accepted the Bill of Rights. She governed during William's campaigns abroad and died of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smallpox">smallpox</a> in 1694.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/mary-ii-of-england.jpg" alt="Mary II of England" width="320" height="522" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Godfrey Kneller · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mary_II_-_Kneller_1690.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
